abstract: The Pacific eDNA Coastal Observatory (PECO) is a coordinated network of
  partners using environmental DNA to track changes in marine biodiversity through
  time. Our network spans 26 degrees latitude (Alaska to Southern California), in
  a cross-national region of high economic and social interest in marine resource
  management. The goals of this project are to develop tools, platforms and networks
  to enable the use of environmental DNA for broad-scale biogeographic assessment,
  build capacity to track biodiversity changes through time, and connect users with
  updatable predictive tools on biodiversity changes. This catalogue entry links to
  the publicly available data collected between 2021-2024.
